/uk/who-is-nathan-cofnas-the-self-styled-race-realist-at-centre-of-jason-arday-plagiarism-row/articleshow/133401581.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T16:08:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133401581,imgsize-731045.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Man dressed as ‘Grim Reaper’ climbs onto hospital roof with long blade and stares at patients]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133401516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/man-dressed-as-grim-reaper-climbs-onto-hospital-roof-with-long-blade-apparently-trying-to-scare-patients/articleshow/133401516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/man-dressed-as-grim-reaper-climbs-onto-hospital-roof-with-long-blade-apparently-trying-to-scare-patients/articleshow/133401516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T16:09:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133401708,imgsize-1127607.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 1,256-megawatt nuclear reactor on Lake Erie accidentally became a wildlife sanctuary, now spotted turtles nest inside its buffer zone]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133401446.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Over the last two centuries, Ohio has witnessed a drastic decline in wetlands, significantly affecting wildlife habitats. However, the land preserved around a nuclear power plant serves as an essential sanctuary for endangered spotted turtles. These turtles thrive in shallow waters rich in vegetation, and the plant's ongoing operations offer a critical generational opportunity for their survival. This unexpected refuge demonstrates nature's remarkable ability to endure amidst human expansion.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-1256-megawatt-nuclear-reactor-on-lake-erie-accidentally-became-a-wildlife-sanctuary-now-spotted-turtles-nest-inside-its-buffer-zone/articleshow/133401446.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-1256-megawatt-nuclear-reactor-on-lake-erie-accidentally-became-a-wildlife-sanctuary-now-spotted-turtles-nest-inside-its-buffer-zone/articleshow/133401446.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T17:07:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133401698,imgsize-132602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1908, Eliza Homans donated 140 acres of land to stop future development, six years later it became a part of Acadia National Park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133397892.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Eliza Homans made a remarkable contribution of 140 acres to establish Acadia National Park, incorporating breathtaking locations like the Bowl and the Beehive. This generous act marked the first significant donation to the Hancock County Trustees of Public Reservation, laying the groundwork for the park's creation. In recognition of her impact, Homans Path was later integrated into the park's expansive trail system, ensuring her legacy persists within its natural beauty.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1908-a-boston-woman-donated-140-acres-around-maines-beehive-and-bowl-to-stop-future-development-six-years-later-5000-acres-had-been-protected-for-what-became-acadia/articleshow/133397892.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1908-a-boston-woman-donated-140-acres-around-maines-beehive-and-bowl-to-stop-future-development-six-years-later-5000-acres-had-been-protected-for-what-became-acadia/articleshow/133397892.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T16:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133397988,imgsize-59144.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Streamer Nitro_Camden’s Twitch stream takes an unexpected turn after StableRonaldo sends 15,000 viewers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133398763.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nitro_Camden, a Twitch streamer, saw his viewer count skyrocket following a raid. However, the celebration was short-lived when his mother barged in, frustrated with the noise, and unplugged his gaming gear. The unexpected showdown became a viral sensation on social media, emphasizing the unpredictable dynamics of live streaming and the impact of personal life on online popularity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/streamer-nitro_camdens-twitch-stream-takes-an-unexpected-turn-after-stableronaldo-sends-15000-viewers/articleshow/133398763.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/streamer-nitro_camdens-twitch-stream-takes-an-unexpected-turn-after-stableronaldo-sends-15000-viewers/articleshow/133398763.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T14:24:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133398812,imgsize-890341.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UAE is turning desert sand into eco-friendly bricks, the method cuts cement needed for construction to nearly half]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133398414.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking study, researchers have engineered eco-friendly bricks using desert sand and various industrial by-products. These bricks boast enhanced sulfate resistance when compared to traditional cement options. An innovative curing process at room temperature minimizes energy use, offering a sustainable alternative to Portland cement. However, further industrial evaluations are essential for these bricks to gain traction in the market.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-is-turning-desert-sand-into-eco-friendly-bricks-and-the-method-cuts-cement-needed-for-construction-to-nearly-half/articleshow/133398414.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-is-turning-desert-sand-into-eco-friendly-bricks-and-the-method-cuts-cement-needed-for-construction-to-nearly-half/articleshow/133398414.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T14:04:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133398455,imgsize-59674.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1962, 5 Swans escaped a Maryland estate; 40 years later, about 4,000 threatened the Bay]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133396440.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Five mute swans escaped from an estate in Maryland in 1962 and their descendants multiplied to nearly 4,000 in the Chesapeake Bay region within four decades. The invasive birds eat large amounts of underwater grasses and have also been linked to the displacement of native birds, raising concerns among wildlife managers about their growing impact on the Bay's ecosystem.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1962-five-pet-mute-swans-escaped-in-maryland-within-four-decades-their-descendants-neared-4000-and-were-eating-10-5-million-pounds-of-chesapeake-bay-grasses-a-year/articleshow/133396440.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1962-five-pet-mute-swans-escaped-in-maryland-within-four-decades-their-descendants-neared-4000-and-were-eating-10-5-million-pounds-of-chesapeake-bay-grasses-a-year/articleshow/133396440.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T14:02:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133397297,imgsize-95424.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[19-year-old Canadian student's invention helps people with cerebral palsy paint and write; sold in 25+ countries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133397385.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Lianna Genovese, a Canadian student, has created an inspiring device called Guided Hands to assist children with cerebral palsy in expressing their creativity through painting. This innovative tool harnesses arm and shoulder movements, enabling young artists to engage with touch screens effectively. Originally composed of basic materials, Guided Hands has transformed into a recognized commercial assistive technology, earning accolades worldwide for its significant impact.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lianna-genovese-an-19-year-old-canadian-student-whose-gadget-made-from-straws-sponge-and-pipes-helps-people-with-cerebral-palsy-rediscover-painting-now-sells-in-over-25-countries/articleshow/133397385.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-lianna-genovese-an-19-year-old-canadian-student-whose-gadget-made-from-straws-sponge-and-pipes-helps-people-with-cerebral-palsy-rediscover-painting-now-sells-in-over-25-countries/articleshow/133397385.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133397744,imgsize-85361.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[N Korea fires 10 missiles amid US scaling back military drills with the South]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133392238.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On Thursday, North Korea fired ten short-range ballistic missiles into eastern waters, a provocative move following the United States' decision to reduce joint military exercises with South Korea. The South Korean military enhanced its monitoring efforts and shared intelligence with its allies. Meanwhile, North Korea dismissed diplomatic outreach from the US President as unworthy of a response. Such missile tests violate United Nations Security Council resolutions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/north-korea-fires-10-missiles-amid-us-scaling-back-military-drills-with-the-south/articleshow/133392238.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/north-korea-fires-10-missiles-amid-us-scaling-back-military-drills-with-the-south/articleshow/133392238.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-21T11:38:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133392238,imgsize-97700.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Angus Johnstone, Australian teacher who flew a kite for 26 hours for charity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133396694.cms" /